{:id :1-l5a004
 :type :claim
 :statement "Under conjugation by $U$, the Pauli expansion of $A = \\sum_P \\hat{a}(P) P$ transforms to $U A U^\\dagger = \\sum_P \\hat{a}(P) (U P U^\\dagger)$. Since $U P U^\\dagger$ spans the Pauli group bijectively (up to phases that don't affect coefficient magnitudes), the squared norm is preserved: $\\|U A U^\\dagger\\|_2^2 = \\|A\\|_2^2$. The Pauli spectral distribution of $U A U^\\dagger$ has $\\pi_{UAU^\\dagger}(Q) = \\pi_A(U^\\dagger Q U)$ where $Q = UPU^\\dagger$ for each $P$."
